                        "entry_id": "b5df4130-30fc-36f3-8a44-58be421672c9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Marked by joy; joyful; joyous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9e4c14c-a4e9-4921-b636-d2c108e6c3b6",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "Such and thousands more are the joysome architectures of nature in contrast to the hurtsome ones of man, but in the last instance they bring us back to the reality that much can be done by combining the forces of nature and those of man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16ebadd4-0828-48e2-a728-8800b3a80d7f",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "But it is a grievous error to see self-sacrificing love in Jesus without remembering that what makes the self-giving of Jesus saving and joysome is the love that restores men to the joy of humanity by the recognition of man by man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fad0fb9c-d9f7-4f91-b6b5-88f42512ad08",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "There is yet a fourth color, the color of gold, which is common to Binah and Gevurah in the mystery of the joysome wine which proceeds to Gevurah from Binah."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ec02bdd-bd09-4770-b242-10138358ec0b",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "From then on, when speaking to other passengers, she referred to him as 'the Doctor', spoke rather disparagingly about the poor people travelling in steerage and warned Jackie, a joysome, pretty six-year-old, still unaware that her stumbling was caused by myopic vision, not to go into that section of the ship for fear that she might become infested with lice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "deb53ff3-453b-4e77-98fa-ed8a5c4ee1e4",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "Oh, this is a fair place to spend eternity. The air smells like honeysuckle. The wind in the pine trees makes a joysome sound."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59893075-b00c-42c0-b4c4-0a57f0c6793a",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "Try to keep the testing time to a joysome minimum so that the people these holes are purportedly being designed for can play, too."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c58d62b-6cb7-40a4-917c-1b4df0f024df",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "Children in bubbling charm / Said \"Freedom is joysome / For we play it in a rhythm\"!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddd9bcdc-5cde-48ae-9848-2643fce114ea",
                                "sense_id": "0adb6c75-6df8-3b07-bd00-88bce67278de",
                                "text": "The house still exudes a joysome, wholesome feeling."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
